main.c
--wide-pointer-encoding
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .* same memory allocated twice: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Wide pointer encoding: two mallocs can return the same address
(address reuse after free). The assertion that they differ is
unsound.
